<title>AUSTRIA: UBS to place CA shares, then leave group.</title>
<headline>UBS to place CA shares, then leave group.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss bank UBS will help place 26 percent of Austria's Creditanstalt-Bankverein shares over the stock exchange and then leave a consortium headed by insurer EA-Generali Aktiengesellschaft AG, an EA-Generali spokesman said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The core consortium has bid for 74 percent (of the state's stake) and will place the remaining 26 percent on the market,&quot; spokesman Josef Hlinka told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;UBS is part of the placement consortium and will not be involved in a possible long-term solution,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom, 43-1-53112-258</p>
</text>
